            <ArticleTitle>Clinical outcome of patients evaluated with emergency centre myocardial perfusion SPET for unexplained chest pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>459-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The clinical outcome of 68 patients with unexplained chest pain triaged with emergency centre (EC) SPET myocardial perfusion imaging (MPI) was assessed at 9 month follow-up. Based on clinical presentation and EC-MPI, 63% (43/68) of patients were discharged from the EC; 84% (36/43) of these patients reported no further symptoms at follow-up. There were no adverse clinical events in patients with totally normal EC-MPI.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
